DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T121700
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Greenhouse + Glassdoor official logins set up
UID:3697bb68-3b7b-4b7c-af62-66a7fdf52880@3697.org
DESCRIPTION:Greenhouse candidate portal (MyGreenhouse) signed in with 
 the\nuser's main email\; sign-in is password-free by emailed code.\nNine 
 prior applications across employers are visible in the\nportal. Glassdoor 
 account created the same day through the\nGoogle sign-in route (the login 
 runs through Indeed one-login\nand offers no password option for this 
 address)\; the Indeed\naccount is linked under the same login. A Gmail 
 draft record\nof the Glassdoor account was deferred by a connector 
 rate\nlimit\; the text is saved for the next mail pass.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T060000
DURATION:PT1H15M
SUMMARY:onlyspx 6am pivots: blocked run recovered\, premarket set posted
UID:4299b283-edab-4685-85db-93daa3ab45b4@4299.org
DESCRIPTION:The scheduled pivots run was blocked on a sign-in wall in 
 the\nworker browser context on all retry-ladder attempts. A manual\nmain-
 chat rerun recovered the day's levels\, and the premarket\npost in the 
 locked format was published and verified on all\nfive channels. The same 
 morning\, both onlyspx scheduled jobs\nwere converted to main-chat 
 execution after the session split\nbetween worker and main-chat browser 
 contexts was confirmed.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T064500
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:MapleScholar morning investigation: PageSpeed day
UID:80c094f2-e0ad-4b89-81a9-3503992d95c3@80c0.org
DESCRIPTION:Read-only investigation completed. A mail sweep for Ads 
 notices\nwas cut off by a connector rate limit\, leaving part of the 
 day\nunseen. Desktop field core-web-vitals failed and worsened on\nthe 
 main section page\, mobile field data was absent across the\nchecked 
 URLs\, and one paper page was a clear lab-performance\noutlier. A 
 discrepancy between the day's top-paper list and the\nprior day's summary 
 was flagged to reconcile. Nothing applied.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261015
SUMMARY:MapleScholar brand search terms pull (read-only)
UID:084bf796-a34e-440d-b000-a72d2504a3da@084b.org
DESCRIPTION:A user-requested pull of search terms and keywords for the 
 two\nbrand-defense campaigns was completed read-only and saved 
 as\nspreadsheets: nothing was added\, paused\, edited\, or 
 excluded.\nFinding: the top matched terms are generic scholarly 
 queries\nrather than brand terms\, matched via broad match\, and the\ntwo-
 word brand keyword exists in exact match only. A separate\ndiagnosis 
 follow-up on the account-level grant daily cap was\npresented with options
  and awaits the user's decision\; no\nbudget or setting was changed.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T073400
DURATION:PT3H
SUMMARY:Shazam library rebuilt as a YouTube Music playlist
UID:093a77e5-52be-46ad-814f-964f32491218@093a.org
DESCRIPTION:The user supplied screenshots of a song-tagging app 
 library\;\n97 unique songs were transcribed and shown in full before 
 any\nadding. Sign-in to the music service on the user's main\naccount was 
 completed first (a stale saved password was\nworked around via a user-
 directed route and a phone\napproval). The playlist build completed after 
 a mid-build\nbrowser outage and resume: 93 tracks added (87 exact 
 matches\,\n6 logged substitutions) and 4 tracks not found on the 
 service\nand logged as such. A web download control exists in-
 browser\;\noffline download on the phone still needs the in-app tap.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T094500
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:onlyspx market-open gap: posted on all channels
UID:a51f5cc9-1200-4d3e-af62-eeee36eb1923@a51f.org
DESCRIPTION:First gap run under main-chat execution\, with no session 
 wall.\nThe gap was computed in the codespace\, the exact draft was\nshown 
 first and approved\, and the text post was published and\nverified on the 
 three text channels\, including the 5-Day Gap\nStatus section. The gap 
 graphic was then published on the two\nimage channels\, completing the 
 day's full onlyspx set.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T091500
DURATION:PT20M
SUMMARY:Proactive handoffs review: surveys presented\, stale items held
UID:1ae715ce-31dc-458c-99ba-48dbf1c7ace5@1ae7.org
DESCRIPTION:Four paid expert survey and interview invitations from 
 recent\nmail were presented to the user in priority order for him to\nrun 
 himself\; nothing was clicked or started. Three prepared\nproactive nudges
  were checked against current records and\nsuppressed as stale. A family 
 travel ticket-issuance item was\nheld in verification pending a passport-
 name confirmation\;\nno reply was sent.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T110000
DURATION:PT15M
SUMMARY:Search Console indexing run: resumed\, one request rejected
UID:c443d3d1-e681-4d73-b60f-dc4fdfde54ed@c443.org
DESCRIPTION:The indexing run was first blocked on a phone approval 
 step\;\nthe user approved and the run resumed from the main chat. The\none
  discovered paper page was inspected and its indexing\nrequest was 
 rejected by the search engine\, which reported a\nfetch failure\, while a 
 direct check minutes later served the\npage normally — a crawler-specific 
 or intermittent failure\,\nnot a down page. The crawled chat URLs were 
 skipped untouched\nunder the permanent owner exclusion. Quota was not hit 
 and\nthe remaining list is unchanged.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T104600
DURATION:PT1H
SUMMARY:Comprehensive perfect-match job search completed: no perfect fits
UID:f9cb31e5-f8a9-4b93-8c1b-c6fb12663b77@f9cb.org
DESCRIPTION:A user-directed comprehensive search was run against 
 the\nmaster v2 resume\, cover letter\, and glossary: 15 domain\nsub-tasks 
 executed strictly sequentially\, Canada city-by-city\nfirst\, then 
 worldwide hubs\, with every candidate verified on\nthe employer's own 
 posting. Result: zero perfect fits\, with\nseveral hundred near-misses 
 each recorded with its exact\nfail reason and coverage gaps stated. One 
 role was flagged\nfor a possible user exception decision. Research only 
 —\nnothing was applied and no employer was contacted.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T130000
DURATION:PT3H
SUMMARY:Special in-platform job search: LinkedIn step complete\, Indeed 
 blocked
UID:a90a6e26-0c08-4191-b7f5-8508aa77a9ee@a90a.org
DESCRIPTION:A second user-directed search worked inside the signed-in\njob 
 platforms step by step\, Canada cities one by one with\nthe location set 
 per city\, judged against the master v2 set.\nThe LinkedIn step completed 
 across all 16 locations with 26\nverified best matches recorded. The 
 Indeed step was blocked\nat its start by a verification check\, left 
 untouched under\nthe standing team rule for the user's own clearance\; 
 the\nremaining platform steps are parked pending that. Research\nonly at 
 this stage — nothing applied.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T160200
DURATION:PT45M
SUMMARY:Deadline application packages built\; first application submitted
UID:1816c0fc-42e8-4039-bddb-5dd014282f02@1816.org
DESCRIPTION:At the user's direction\, tailored application packages 
 were\nbuilt for four time-sensitive health and research roles\nclosing 
 over three days. The first application was submitted\nthrough the 
 employer's directed email channel in its required\nformat and logged in 
 the tracker with a seven-day follow-up.\nThe second was blocked at a 
 candidate-account creation wall\;\nthe user later directed which existing 
 password to use for\nthat account. The remaining two routes were mapped 
 as\naccount-required application portals\, packages ready.
DTSTAMP:20261014T222559Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261014T170000
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Icarus appraisal replies watch: no new replies
UID:661f46d9-6157-42b5-a400-09f2f2ce4bca@661f.org
DESCRIPTION:The replies watch checked the mailbox live for responses 
 from\nthe auction houses and appraiser contacted about the bronze.\nNo new
  replies: one house has declined\, one is still reviewing\nwith its team\,
  and two parties remain silent. No estimate has\nbeen received yet and the
  watch continues on schedule.
